WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:07.379
I'm gonna start by just pointing out some
of the symbolism in the movie, then at the

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:11.620
end I'll piece it all together and let you
know how the religious subplot ties into the

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.539
surface level story about the author and his
wife.

00:00:14.539 --> 00:00:18.900
Let me start off by saying that different
audiences are going to have different interpretations

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:19.900
of this movie.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.920
This is just my interpreation, so if your
view on the movie isn't the same as mine...

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.269
THEN SCREW YOU, IDIOT.

00:00:26.269 --> 00:00:30.849
So with that all out of the way, I see the
movie as a representation of The Exodus.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:36.440
Long story short, back in the day the Israelites
were enslaved by the Pharaoh in Egypt.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.100
There was this dude named Moses.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.940
God hits him up and says he's going to drop
these plagues on the Egyptians to force them

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.430
to let his people go.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.540
There were 10 Plagues in all.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.039
These events are the basis for the Jewish
holiday, Passover.

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:52.210
Each of these 10 plagues are represented in
Darren Aronofsky's film.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.280
The first plague was the plague of blood.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.100
In the Exodus, all the water in Egypt is turned
into blood -- in mother!

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.629
the two brothers barge into the house and
start arguing about their father's will.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:03.809
This leads to a physical fight resulting in
a death.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:10.210
The living room, or in this case, the dying
room, is covered in a pool of blood, and no

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:14.640
matter what Jennifer Lawrence does, she can't
get the blood to fully go away, much like

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.110
another horror movie that came out this year.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.520
The blood seeps down into the cellar, and
follows this path along the wall, which shows

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.200
us that this isn't just a regular leak, there
is something of a divine interference.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.280
This part may or may not be related, but when
the water in Egypt was turned to blood, the

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.240
Egyptians suffered from terrible thirst.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.100
When Ed Harris gets to the house, Jennifer
Lawrence offers him some tea, she gets back

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.229
from making it to find that they've already
broken into a flask of alcohol, not to mention

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.370
Michelle Pfeiffer's crazy obsession with making
lemonade.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.140
So this could mirror the thirst of the Egyptians.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.060
The basement is the setting for the appearance
of several of the plagues.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.960
I also like the idea of the blood being something
that is literally sent from above, and in

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:00.229
the Exodus, the Egyptians tried digging into
the ground to find water, only to find more

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:05.170
blood, similar to how Jennifer goes underground
into the basement and finds more blood there

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:06.450
was well.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:10.660
It's also worth noting that Moses makes the
blood first appear by striking the Nile river

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.600
with a wooden staff, and the blood in mother!

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.420
appears after the brother strikes his sibling
with a wooden chair.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.270
The second plague is frogs.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.769
The Egyptians' houses were invaded by these
swarms of frogs.

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:26.290
Right after she goes into the basement to
follow the blood, there is this wall that

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.050
she breaks away and it leads her to a secret
area, where she finds a frog living in her

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.050
basement.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.530
It wasn't a swarm of frogs, but it's just
more of a subtle reference.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.910
Plus, where there is one amphibian, there
are usually more to be found.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:43.980
The only plague that I'm not entirely sure
about is the third one, which is lice / bugs.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:48.101
It's likely that this plague is represented
somewhere in the movie considering that the

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:52.290
other 9 are accounted for but I wasn't really
looking out for them when watching this for

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.290
the first time.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:57.010
If you have ideas about this one, let me know
in the comments, I'd love to fill in that

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.230
missing piece.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.840
But anyway, the fourth plague is accounted
for.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.450
When Javier Bardem offers to hold the wake
for the deceased son of Ed Harris, the house

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:10.630
is overrun by seemingly tons of random guests
and these guests represent the horde of wild

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.630
beasts.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:16.380
In the Exodus passage, the beasts are described
as wild animals that rove all over the country

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.600
and destroy everything that they have built.

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.400
Our two main characters have spent their marriage
renovating this house together and these people

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:26.560
literally roam in in hordes and destroy what
they have built together.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.010
The fifth plague involved a disease that killed
all of the Egyptians' livestock.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.700
Jennifer and Javier aren't shown to have any
livestock, but there is a scene in the kitchen

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.220
where she sees a dying bee keel over and pass
away.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.570
This is the most relevant modern world parallel
to diseased livestock.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.480
Beekeeping is an industry where colonies are
maintained by man in order to collect and

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:51.199
sell the natural products that the bee produces,
one that has been threatened in recent years

00:03:51.199 --> 00:03:55.230
by a mysterious disease killing up to 50%
of bees.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:59.570
In this case, bees represent the livestock
of these beekeepers and the colony collapse

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.449
disorder is a modern day plague against them.

00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:07.250
The sixth plague was boils, which manifest
the first night that Ed Harris stays over

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.259
at the house.

00:04:08.259 --> 00:04:12.750
He gets sick and Jennifer Lawrence hears him
coughing as she is trying to get to sleep.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.320
She gets up to see if everything is alright
and finds her husband tending to him.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.280
He is coughing and vomiting over the toilet
and seems to be covered in painful looking

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.450
boils.

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.620
When she asks him about it the next day, he
claims to be fine.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:30.270
In addition to that, here is the actual quote
from the Exodus passage: "Take handfuls of

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:35.810
soot from a furnace and have Moses toss it
into the air in the presence of Pharaoh.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:42.180
It will become fine dust over the whole land
of Egypt, and festering boils will break out

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.040
on men and animals throughout the land."

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.040
— Exodus 9:8–9

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.320
The movie has a strong emphasis on the furnace
in the basement.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.260
At first I thought it was a throwback to the
refrigerator in Aronofsky's 2000 film, Requiem

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:57.470
for a Dream, just because of the fact that
it's a large appliance that makes noises that

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:02.220
scare her and at that point in the film it
seemed like it was possibly a hallucination.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.670
However, looking back on it, there may have
been a deeper significance.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:11.630
Later in the movie, we actually see this furnace
soot stuff being plastered on Javier Bardem's

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.630
followers.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.200
The seventh plague is a thunderstorm of hail.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.760
Again, this isn't represented with a literal
halestorm, but rather a scaled down representation.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.750
This comes up during the wake scene, and despite
Jennifer Lawrence's constant requests, people

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.880
keep sitting on her sink countertop, which
has not yet been reinforced.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:35.060
Eventually, the counter snaps, the pipe breaks
and a storm of water sprays up and begins

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.060
flooding the house, creating complete chaos.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:42.150
Jennifer Lawrence even refers to the mess
created by these people as an "apocalypse",

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:47.880
a reference to the apocalyptic conditions
of the aforementioned hailstorm.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.240
[Clip]

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.750
No, not that halestorm.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.950
Moving right along plague 8, we have the locusts.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:57.840
After the thunderstorm, God's message for
Pharaoh, was this:

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:03.200
"If you refuse to let them go, I will bring
locusts into your country tomorrow.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.540
They will cover the face of the ground so
that it cannot be seen.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.370
They will devour what little you have left
after the hail...

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:15.170
They will fill your houses and those of all
your officials and all the Egyptians."

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:16.170
— Exodus 10:3–6

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:18.270
I see the representation of the locusts in
mother!

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.620
to be the fans of Javier Bardem.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.950
They invade the house, literally to the point
that the floor cannot be seen.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:28.760
They devour all of the food, including the
meal that Jennifer Lawrence had just prepared,

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:31.840
and they take everything that remains, ripping
the house apart to get a piece of their hero's

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:32.840
life.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.930
That situation continues to devolve until
there is a full on war taking place in the

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:40.100
house, complete with soldiers and riot police.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:44.420
It is at this point that Jennifer Lawrence
is temporarily blinded, she gets sprayed in

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.440
the face with pepper spray.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.920
Enter plague number 9: Darkness.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:54.050
And of course, this all culminates with the
tenth and final plague: Death of the first

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.050
born.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:58.590
Jennifer Lawrence finally delivers her baby,
Javier Bardem gives it to the people, their

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:01.510
careless actions lead to the baby's neck snapping.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:07.410
Now that I've identified the 10 plagues, or
at least 9 of the 10, I'll let the director,

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:12.310
Darren Aronofsky, explain the roles of the
characters and their relationship to the religious

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:13.310
figures.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:18.620
"Using to tell the stories of humanity, the
stories of the bible.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:29.320
Ed and Michelle are the first man and woman,
and these are the sons.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:33.660
And you can probably then figure out who Javier
is from that last shot."

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.680
So with that in mind, let's take a look back
at the scene in the study.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.770
When Ed Harris first sees the... uh...

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.290
I'm just gonna call it the shiny object, he
is captivated by it.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:48.890
He feels this need to hold it, to touch it,
but Javier tells him that the shiny object

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:53.370
is very precious to him and forbids him from
touching it, going so far as to say no guests

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.890
will be allowed in the study while he is not
in there.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:08:01.020
The shiny object is our metaphorical apple
of Eden, but Ed and Michelle, being the Adam

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:06.330
and Eve that they are go in there anyway and
break it, and then God is pretty upset and

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:10.810
he forever bans them from the Garden of Eden
by boarding off the area with hammer and nails.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:15.630
They retreat to their room and the next time
we see them, they are doing it.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:19.650
Next thing you know, they have kids, who show
up to the house, Cain and Abel.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:23.710
Cain is the older brother, thought to be the
originator of all things evil and violent,

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:28.780
so shoutout to him, he slays his younger brother
Abel, and the family proceeds to grieve, and

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:34.150
it's during this time that they turn to God
/ Javier Bardem, who gives a speech at the

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:35.969
wake that offers them hope.

00:08:35.969 --> 00:08:40.320
This leads to him gaining a huge following
and these people become his worshippers.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.000
He writes a holy scripture...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.099
aka: his book.

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:46.990
However, some of them are led astray, and
worship a false idol, which we see when people

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:50.690
are worshipping a photo, or his possessions,
rather than the real thing.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.650
That's kind of where the 10 Plagues thing
comes in.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:57.870
The Egyptians worship the Pharaoh, a false
God, while Jews worship their one only.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:03.110
The Jewish people escape Egypt, are promised
the Holy Land of Israel by God, but there

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:07.190
are also the Palestinians who also claim the
divine right to that land.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:11.550
So a huge fight breaks out, which we see in
the movie, starting as the followers of Javier

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:16.660
arguing over who gets to be in the house,
which eventually becomes who gets his possessions,

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:22.740
and continues to devolve into a full blown
war zone representative of the ongoing Israeli-Palestine

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.740
conflict.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.400
Finally, Jennifer has the baby and all of
Javier's followers are waiting outside to

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.460
see the newborn.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.460
You could look at this as the birth of Christianity,
with the baby being Jesus and dying for the

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:36.580
people's sins, or you could examine Jennifer's
actions, sheltering the baby for many days

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:41.710
and nights, asking Javier, the Pharaoh, the
false God, to make those people go before

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:43.370
he holds the child.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:48.050
Very similar to Moses asking Pharaoh to let
my people go and also aligning with the Torah

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:53.089
story of the Israelites escaping from Egypt
and wandering the desert for 40 years to let

00:09:53.089 --> 00:09:58.210
the generation that was tainted by Pharaoh
die off so that a new, pure generation could

00:09:58.210 --> 00:09:59.839
enter the promised land.

00:09:59.839 --> 00:10:04.640
The new iteration of the cycle could represent
a new beginning in that promised land.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.540
Or it could represent the opening of a new
book, the new testament.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.279
It all depends how you look at it.

00:10:10.279 --> 00:10:11.860
And I think that's the point.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:16.080
As with real life, there are different people
with different beliefs, and this is the cause

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.290
for different religions.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.750
That's my interpretation of the subtext, but
what does it have to do with the surface level

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:24.550
story -- the one about a writer and his wife
trying to have a baby?

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:29.540
I think Aronofsky is comparing our current
celebrity crazed culture to the worship of

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:30.610
false idols.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:34.630
When Ed Harris gets to the house, he poses
as a doctor who has lost his way looking for

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.110
a place to stay.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:41.230
Jennifer later finds a picture of her husband
in the man's bag from the about me section

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:42.910
of one of his books.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:47.780
The man confesses to being a superfan who
came out just to see Javier before he passes

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:48.780
away.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:52.570
Javier says that it's nice to have someone
who appreciates his writing, to which Jennifer

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.390
responds, "I love your work."

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:59.400
This creates the divide between someone who
loves him for who he is and someone who worships

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.190
the idea of him, his celebrity persona.

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:06.550
Ed becomes so enthralled by his idol that
he brings his wife along to meet him.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:11.190
After the unfortunate passing of the man's
son, Javier offers hospitality and words of

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.570
wisdom in front of a large group of people
and his cult following grows.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:20.020
After releasing his next scripture, he has
fans waiting outside his house to meet him,

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:24.610
and before long, that turns into breaking
into his house, people fighting over him,

00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:27.590
tossing all of their morals for a chance to
meet him.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:32.140
Aronofsky is commenting on how modern obsession
over celebrities has become like a religious

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:33.140
craze.

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:36.650
People worship these celebrities and look
at the damage that it causes.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:41.330
As far as I noticed, not one of the characters
in the movie is given an actual name, so we

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:45.970
have to refer to them using the name of the
actor, as I have throughout this entire video.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:49.310
This practice feeds into the whole idolisation
of celebrities.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:52.670
People are so obsessed with these actors that
they ignore everything else.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:56.130
Have you ever referred to a movie character
in conversation, not been able to remember

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.990
the name and said something like "the Jennifer
Lawrence-character"?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:04.600
By not giving the characters names, this is
exactly the behaviour that Aronofsky is trying

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:05.600
to highlight.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:06.600
Look up mother!

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.600
on Google right now.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:11.670
You'll notice several articles referring to
the movie as Jennifer Lawrence's new movie

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:12.670
mother!

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:16.750
As you know by now, the film was directed
by Darren Aronofsky.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:18.700
Not Jennifer Lawrence.

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:23.290
But speaking of Jennifer Lawrence, what an
ideal candidate for a movie about the damage

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:25.280
caused by the obsession of celebrities.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:29.510
A few years ago she had her iCloud hacked
and nude photos leaked to the internet in

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.589
an incident known as the Fappening.

00:12:31.589 --> 00:12:34.851
To be entirely transparent though, she may
have just been casted because she's sleeping

00:12:34.851 --> 00:12:36.110
with the director.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.880
Literally, she is.

